        rules: {
          objective: 'Accurately bid and then win the number of tricks promised over a sequence of changing hand sizes.',
          gameplay: 'Deal a changing number of cards each hand, turn or determine trump according to the table rule, and have players bid expected tricks. Players then play tricks clockwise, following suit when able; trumps and especially the two Jokers outrank ordinary suit cards. Score each hand from the relation between bid tricks and tricks actually won.',
          keyRules: [
            'The 52-card deck is supplemented by two Jokers called Blukes, which are the top trumps.',
            'Hand size changes from deal to deal, so bidding strength must be recalculated every round.',
            'Players follow suit when able; otherwise they may trump or discard according to normal trick-taking practice.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus first on the visible objective in Bluke: conserve cards or resources that directly advance the win condition.',
